# Toast, errors, and TanStack Query

## Toast API
- Use `toast.success` / `toast.error` / `toast.info` / `toast.warning` from `@/components/ui/toast`.
- Do not use raw `toast({ title, variant })` in new or migrated code.

## Errors and success
- Errors: `handleErrorWithToast(t('domain.action.error'), error)`.
- Success after mutations: `toast.success(t('domain.action.success'))` in the page
  `try/catch` around `mutateAsync` (not inside mutation composables).

## TanStack Query
- Reference domain: `src/domains/contractor/composables/`.
- Per domain: `queryKeys.ts`, `use<Domain>Queries.ts`, `use<Domain>Mutations.ts`.
- Mutations invalidate query keys only; pages own toasts and navigation.
- List/detail loading comes from `isPending` / `isError` / `refetch` — no local
  `loading = ref(false)` for API reads.
- Pinia holds client/UI selection state only, not list/detail server caches.
